// Title: Potential Russian APT Credential Theft Activity
// Sigma ID: b83f5166-9237-4b5e-9cd4-7b5d52f4d8ee
// Status: stable | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-02-21 | Modified: 2023-03-08
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552.001, T1003.003
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects Russian group activity as described in Global Threat Report 2019 by Crowdstrike
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/5743766-Global-Threat-Report-2019.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2019/TA/Bear-APT-Activity/proc_creation_win_apt_bear_activity_gtr19.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "xcopy /S /E /C /Q /H \\\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\sysvol\\") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "adexplorer -snapshot \"\" c:\\users\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\downloads\\" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".snp")
